<title>KUWAIT: Kuwait import payments fell 17.9 pct in June.</title>
<headline>Kuwait import payments fell 17.9 pct in June.</headline>
<dateline>KUWAIT 1996-09-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Payments made by Kuwaiti banks to finance imports rose 17.9 percent to 121.8 million dinars in June from 148.5 million dinars in May, a Central Bank monthly bulletin said.</p>
<p>The payments were 115.8 million dinars in June 1995.</p>
<p>			   Figures in millions of dinars</p>
<p>				     June	  May	 June '95</p>
<p>Documentary LCs		   81.2	 102.3	79.1</p>
<p>Bills for collection	    17.1	  23.1	18.1</p>
<p>Other payment orders	    23.4	  23.2	18.5</p>
<p>The relative importance of the U.S. dollar in the financing fell to 61.5 percent in June from 64.2 in May. That of the Japanese yen fell to 4.2 percent from 5.3 percent.</p>
<p>Slight discrepancies in figures are due to rounding.</p>
<p>($1 = 0.2999 dinars)</p>
<p>-- Inal Ersan, Kuwait newsroom +965 243 1920</p>
